    {
      "id": "q31-Puu_cjk4oqIYnqPpI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 874.7910474095271,
      "y": 1687.7702773114106,
      "width": 2241.03857421875,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aK",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 866026754,
      "version": 1419,
      "versionNonce": 1055058818,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1757441547406,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Here\n1. Route53 means configurations of domain name with urls and adding SSL certificate to make it secure\n2. Amplify : deploy aour frontend application\n3.React app will be communicaating with https(route 53) protocol via ALB to distribute load on backend server(if load exceed on one server than spawn a new backend server\n4.backedn server is storing some objects like images,invoices etc to s3 ,the react application can directly acess the s3 using some kind of signed url. which we are going to expose to fronted appliaction via cloudfront distribution \n5. here elastic search is used to avoid expensive calls to rds beacuse user can perform lots of search query like searching keywords,finding products,finding keywords etc etc.\n6. while we creating products,updating products we are indexing these specific documents in elastic search so our fronted can access it via two routes\n7. we have rd where we will be using postgres and it can be sharaded according to need like read db,write db\n8. 3rd party: notifications.email,pdf,invoice etc\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Here\n1. Route53 means configurations of domain name with urls and adding SSL certificate to make it secure\n2. Amplify : deploy aour frontend application\n3.React app will be communicaating with https(route 53) protocol via ALB to distribute load on backend server(if load exceed on one server than spawn a new backend server\n4.backedn server is storing some objects like images,invoices etc to s3 ,the react application can directly acess the s3 using some kind of signed url. which we are going to expose to fronted appliaction via cloudfront distribution \n5. here elastic search is used to avoid expensive calls to rds beacuse user can perform lots of search query like searching keywords,finding products,finding keywords etc etc.\n6. while we creating products,updating products we are indexing these specific documents in elastic search so our fronted can access it via two routes\n7. we have rd where we will be using postgres and it can be sharaded according to need like read db,write db\n8. 3rd party: notifications.email,pdf,invoice etc\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "LBDLLluQpzSJIfIU8k3EN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 864.7767944661946,
      "y": 2028.2958236716372,
      "width": 1325.8990478515625,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
